# pstack model routing (verified 2026-08-15)

pstack ships defaults this environment does not have. A `Task` call naming a missing slug fails, so
these overrides are not preference — they are the available set, confirmed by probing a live agent:

| pstack role | pstack default | USE HERE |
|---|---|---|
| judgment / prose | `claude-fable-5-thinking-max` | `claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh` |
| precise instruction-following | `gpt-5.6-sol-max` | `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` |
| fast mechanical code | `grok-4.6-fast-xhigh` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` |

Available `model` values observed on a cloud agent: `inherit`, `claude-fable-5-thinking-high`,
`claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh`, `claude-opus-5-thinking-high`, `claude-opus-5-thinking-high-fast`,
`claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high`, plus composer variants.

Subagent types available to `Task`: `generalPurpose`, `explore`, `debug`, `computerUse`,
`videoReview`, `cursor-guide`, `best-of-n-runner`.

⚠️ If a `Task` call errors on an unknown model, drop the `model` argument and let it inherit rather
than guessing another slug.
